format session-log-v1
stamp 20260906.210117
editor Claude Code, Zed-class CLI on the pier
provider Anthropic
product Claude Code
role incense seat -- law, active-designing, iterative review, the captain's hat
modality text
model claude-opus-5
model_status active runtime reported by the harness environment block
voice Kyri
host Linux pier, 8 vCPU / 16 GB, TZ America/New_York
title The rule that was written and never formed
prompt Keaton: keep the same account, restart all the fleet loops, and kg incense here.
think The fleet first: seven ships and the watch relaunched bare, every one confirmed to have found its lane rather than counted as a process. The four diverged lines parked by name -- pier/diverged-20260906-210007 on three trees -- which is round-open doing exactly what it promises.
think Then the lap. The card carries a question left explicitly to incense and marked its FOURTEENTH firing: should an OPEN row carry a claim, a seat and a stamp, at START. Fourteen firings of one question is a loom waiting to be built, and it is law, which is this seat's own lane.
think I read the law before designing anything, and the answer was already in it. derived-spine rule 4, seated 20260827: cite by stamp until the row is shared. The row ALREADY carries a stamp at start; the stamp is the claim. A distributed lock would move the collision earlier rather than remove it.
think So the measurable question was whether rule 4 is obeyed, and it is not. Every session log from today cites a number the spine had yet to bind; none reached for the stamp.
obs THE RENUMBERING WAS NEVER THE COST, AND THAT REFRAMES FOURTEEN FIRINGS. The stamp held in all 28 recorded errata -- the law working exactly as designed. What costs is every OTHER file that spelled the number, and a %N reaches 20 to 36 files within a day of being written. One such sweep ran as a blind sed that rewrote a peer's row and two upstream passages. Six rows renumbered more than once, one four times in an hour.
obs A HEX COLOUR TAUGHT THE PATTERN ITS BOUNDARY. My first regex read %[0-9]{3,4} and matched a PREFIX of %200000 in two image modules -- a very dark red, not a ledger row. The pattern takes the whole run of digits now and measures its length afterward, which is the same right-side boundary the reference census learned one law over.
obs THREE ROOMS ARE READ PAST AND EACH FOR A DIFFERENT REASON. The ledger ASSIGNS a number rather than citing one, so REDS.md and its shelves are exempt by definition. Testimony RECORDS what the number was when written. And a five-digit run is a colour. Three exclusions, three reasons, none of them a waiver.
obs THE FOLD SHELF FOUND ITS OWN CLAUSE AND IT WAS THE DAY'S SHAPE. %489, %508 and %509 all read BOOKED and all three are one fault: selecting a thing by a name something else also answers to. A room name a second filter also matched, a filename three running prompts contained, a row number the remote had yet to allocate. A name is only a selector while nothing else carries it.
loom census session_logs_read=40 cited_by_number=40 cited_by_stamp=0
loom ledger errata=28 rows_renumbered_twice_plus=6 worst_row=4_renumbers citation_reach=20_to_36_files
loom control unshared_citation pass=10 fail=0 stub_spine=yes
loom pin reds_bytes=43002 ceiling=40960 after_fold=37872 rows_folded=3
file tools/fixtures/r/unshared_citation_scan.sh the census -- shared_max from the spine, citations above it held at zero
file tools/r/unshared_citation_witness.rish the guard, rostered tier lap
file tools/fixtures/r/unshared_citation_control.sh ten behaviors against a stub spine, every refusal planted then lifted
file .claude/rules/derived-spine.md rule 4 made a gate, with the bill measured and the three exclusions reasoned
file construction/REDS.md %513 booked; %489, %508 and %509 folded under the clause they share
scope the fourteenth firing answered by reading the law rather than designing a lock, and rule 4 made checkable
status GREEN -- unshared_citation 10 of 10 and zero citations, reds monotone, fold and shelf-link green, tracked links ok
recommend keep-going -- the standing question is closed by measurement; the next incense door is the mycelium negatives one, also left to this seat.
